## Working contract

- State the goal, constraints, relevant context, and “done when” before editing.
- Read the smallest live source and classify the change risk.
- Use Plan mode for ambiguous, cross-system, migration, trust-boundary, or
  release work.
- Prefer the simplest reversible implementation and existing project patterns.
- Run the closest focused check, then self-review every change.
- Request one bounded independent review for runtime, data, security,
  authentication, migration, or release risk.
- Prepare evidence and remaining risks, then stop for human merge approval.
- Treat incomplete harness alignment as advisory and report at most one material
  improvement without displacing the requested task.

## Evidence boundaries

Label results as implemented, locally verified, browser verified, Preview
verified, Production verified, provider verified, or unverified. Never infer
deployment or provider state from local checks or stored artifacts.

## Human gates

Obtain explicit approval before merge, Production or provider mutation, secrets
or privilege changes, destructive actions, material cost, or external
communication.

## Done condition

The requested scope is complete, the closest sufficient validation has passed,
the diff has been self-reviewed, evidence is accurately labeled, and remaining
risk or unverified state is reported.
